WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:11.920
Messier 36 or M36, also known as NGC 1960 or the Pinwheel Cluster, is an open cluster of stars in the somewhat northern constellation Auriga.

00:12.521 --> 00:19.304
It was discovered by Giovanni Batista Hodierna before 1654, who described it as a nebulous patch.

00:19.855 --> 00:30.105
The cluster was independently re-discovered by Guillaume Le Gentil in 1749, then Charles Messier observed it in 1764 and added it to his catalogue.

00:30.616 --> 00:34.965
It is about 1,330 pc away from Earth.

00:35.476 --> 00:43.383
The cluster is very similar to the Pleiades cluster (M45), and if as far away it would be of similar apparent magnitude.
